---
import PolicyLayout from '../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Shop Terms"
  description="The terms that apply to orders placed through the Cloud Peptides shop."
  lastUpdated="August 8, 2026"
>
  <h2>An order request is not an accepted order</h2>
  <p>
    Submitting the cart form creates an order <strong>request</strong>. It does not create
    acceptance of an order, charge you, reserve inventory, or guarantee fulfillment. We review every
    request and contact you directly afterward to proceed. Nothing is purchased or sold until we do.
  </p>

  <h2>Research use only</h2>
  <p>
    Everything in our shop is sold for laboratory research use only and is not for human
    consumption. No claims of safety or effectiveness for human use are made or implied. See our
    full <a href="/disclaimer">Research and Medical Disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Eligibility</h2>
  <p>You must be at least 18 years old to submit an order request.</p>

  <h2>Legal status is your responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    Laws governing research chemicals and peptides vary by location. It is your responsibility to
    know and follow the laws that apply to you before submitting an order request.
  </p>

  <h2>No payment is collected through this website</h2>
  <p>
    This site does not collect or process payment of any kind — no card, bank, or cryptocurrency
    information is requested or accepted anywhere on this website. Submitting an order request never
    charges you. If a request is accepted, payment is arranged directly between you and us, outside
    this website's systems, after that acceptance.
  </p>

  <h2>Batch testing (COAs)</h2>
  <p>
    We publish batch testing documentation (Certificates of Analysis) for applicable products in our <a
      href="/coas">COA gallery</a
    >. COA documentation is a commerce record of batch testing — it is not scientific evidence, and
    it is never cited within our published research claims. See our full <a href="/disclaimer"
      >Research and Medical Disclaimer</a
    > for how research claims and commerce information are kept separate.
  </p>

  <h2>Pricing and availability</h2>
  <p>
    Prices and product availability shown in the shop are subject to change and are not a binding
    offer — an order request is only reviewed against current pricing and availability at the time
    we act on it.
  </p>

  <h2>Shipping and returns</h2>
  <p>
    See our <a href="/shipping">Shipping Policy</a> (order minimums, shipping cost, and the customs replacement
    guarantee) and <a href="/returns">Return and Refund Policy</a> (all sales final, except where required
    by law).
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/contact">Contact us</a> with any question about an order request or these terms.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
